Third-party software and sources
--------------------------------

Version 0.1 is a map of analysis pathways and runs no analyses. The map
describes, and later releases will call, the following R packages. Each is
distributed under its own license; cite them as their authors ask, by running
citation("<package>") in R.

  metafor     https://cran.r-project.org/package=metafor
              Viechtbauer W (2010). Conducting meta-analyses in R with the
              metafor package. Journal of Statistical Software, 36(3), 1-48.
  meta        https://cran.r-project.org/package=meta
  netmeta     https://cran.r-project.org/package=netmeta
  bayesmeta   https://cran.r-project.org/package=bayesmeta
  mada        https://cran.r-project.org/package=mada
  metamisc    https://cran.r-project.org/package=metamisc
  dosresmeta  https://cran.r-project.org/package=dosresmeta

The methodological content of the map cites the Cochrane Handbook for
Systematic Reviews of Interventions (https://www.cochrane.org/authors/handbooks-and-manuals/handbook)
and the documentation of the packages above. Every source used is listed, with
its link, in spec/backbone.md.

